//@version=6

// Futures are margined, and the broker emulator is not: left alone it wants
// the whole notional in cash, which one MNQ contract already exceeds, and
// every order is rejected without a word. Two percent is fifty to one, which
// is what a broker's day margin on a micro looks like. MARGIN_PCT in the
// portfolio mirrors this number; change both or neither.
// Every order carries its own qty, sized by risk management, so Properties'
// default order size is never read. Declared in contracts anyway: left at a
// percentage of equity it reads like a second risk setting, and changing it
// does nothing.
strategy("Node - v2.0.0-dev.1", overlay = true, initial_capital = 50000,
     margin_long = 2, margin_short = 2,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500)